% C6-FLOUT: FLOAT OUTPUT.  .ERRCHK (FLOAT:190) WANTS DIGITS NOT BELOW ZERO,
% A FIELD ABOVE ZERO AND A FIELD WIDER THAN THE DIGITS.  .SELECT (FLOAT:200)
% PADS WITH (ROOM - EXPONENT) BLANKS AND CONVERTS THE SMALLER OF THE ROOM
% AND THE EXPONENT, SO A NUMBER TOO WIDE FOR ITS FIELD LOSES DIGITS.  E=
% TAKES FOUR COLUMNS FOR THE EXPONENT.  .<#> GIVES FOUR FRACTION DIGITS.
% DIGITS ARE TRUNCATED, NOT ROUNDED.  A NUMBER WITH TOO MANY INTEGER DIGITS
% FOR ITS FIELD GETS AN EXPONENT AND RUNS PAST THE FIELD.  ZERO IS NOT
% NEGATIVE (DEFECT 47), AND THE DIGITS ARE DECIMAL IN ANY RADIX (48).
% EACH FIELD IS PRINTED BETWEEN BARS.  AN ERROR ENDS ITS LINE.
FLOAT< DECIMAL
() I_ABORT ABORT !
'FB : "|" MSG F= "|" MSG ;
'EB : "|" MSG E= "|" MSG ;
'GB : "|" MSG .<#> TYPE "|" MSG ;
"F 10 3  " MSG 3.14159 10 3 FB 0. 10 3 FB -2.5 10 3 FB 1. 10 0 FB CR
"F 5 3   " MSG 3.14159 5 3 FB -3.14159 6 3 FB CR
"F 4 3   " MSG 3.14159 4 3 FB "NOT REACHED" MSG CR
"F 3 3   " MSG 3.14159 3 3 FB "NOT REACHED" MSG CR
"F 0 0   " MSG 3.14159 0 0 FB "NOT REACHED" MSG CR
"F 5 -1  " MSG 3.14159 5 -1 FB "NOT REACHED" MSG CR
"F 1 0   " MSG 3.14159 1 0 FB 7. 2 0 FB CR
"F WIDE  " MSG 1234.5 8 1 FB 1234.5 7 1 FB 1234.5 6 1 FB 1234.5 5 1 FB CR
"F NEG   " MSG -1234.5 8 1 FB -1234.5 7 1 FB -1234.5 6 1 FB CR
"F SMALL " MSG 0.001 8 4 FB 0.0001 8 4 FB 0.00001 8 4 FB 0.5 4 2 FB CR
"F 10^9  " MSG 10. 9. .^ 14 2 FB 10. 9. .^ 11 2 FB 10. 9. .^ 12 0 FB CR
"E 12 3  " MSG 3.14159 12 3 EB 10. 9. .^ 12 3 EB 0.001 12 3 EB -2.5 12 3 EB CR
"E 8 3   " MSG 3.14159 8 3 EB "NOT REACHED" MSG CR
"E 9 3   " MSG 3.14159 9 3 EB 3.14159 7 1 EB CR
"G       " MSG 0. GB 1. GB -1. GB 123.456 GB 0.001 GB 10. 20. .^ GB CR
"G HEX   " MSG HEX 255. GB 0.5 GB 10. 20. .^ 8 2 FB 10. 20. .^ 12 2 EB 0. 8 2 EB DECIMAL CR
"STACKS  " MSG 99 = 1.5 .= CR
